insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('b9b22896-8d5f-4ca5-939a-6d04c112efe3', '70fd6c98-17f2-4e56-be6c-cea7055fb759', 'Self-doubt gets a bad reputation. In leadership, in startups', 0, 'Self-doubt gets a bad reputation. In leadership, in startups, in decision-making - it’s usually labeled as a flaw.

But over the past year, I’ve realized that if you recognize it and apply it wisely, self-doubt can actually be a strength.

Here’s how I use it:

1) Double-checking solutions: “What if there’s a better approach?” or “Did I miss something?”
2) Polishing outcomes: Re-examining decisions often leads to stronger results.
3) Mindful application: The key is awareness - don’t overthink, but don’t ignore your doubts.

In running a wellness tech startup, every small improvement matters.
Self-doubt, when controlled, is not paralysis.

It’s a tool that helps me build better solutions for our users and strengthen our processes at CipherCross.

Leadership isn’t about never doubting yourself.
It’s about using your doubts to fuel better decisions.

ð¡How do you turn challenges or doubts into an advantage in your work?

<https://www.figma.com/design/ghrgcaInRycN4UJ29mgRUJ/Mykyta--1--Posts?node-id=0-1&t=rETsVPNqngMJsUY8-1>', 'https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mykyta-shevchenko-ciphercross-wellness_self-doubt-gets-a-bad-reputation-in-leadership-activity-7440298559100522496-ECKf?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAACKi8XsB9WBoWK1z6g7nRgrBaW3-4QoyJT8', 'posted', '2026-03-19T09:00:00Z', '2026-03-19T09:00:00Z');
